  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Brasfield and Gorrie obligated $416M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Brasfield and Gorrie received 16 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $26M. Brasfield and Gorrie saw obligations down 5.8% year over year. The Department of Homeland Security is the largest buyer of Brasfield and Gorrie work in FY2026 to date at $326M, followed by the Department of Defense at $59.6M and the General Services Administration at $21.1M. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is Brasfield and Gorrie’s largest market at $416M. The record shows smaller activity in Engineering Services at $200K and minor or negative entries in other NAICS categories, reflecting concentrated federal demand in building construction.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Brasfield and Gorrie’s federal business changed over time?",
        "body": "Brasfield and Gorrie’s obligations rose and fell across the last six fiscal years, with FY23 at $679M and FY24 at $587M. Brasfield and Gorrie’s obligations were $442M in FY25 and are $416M in FY26 to date, down 5.8% year over year. Brasfield and Gorrie’s FY21 and FY22 totals were $178M and $154M respectively, showing that recent federal activity is larger than the early years in the series."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who buys from Brasfield and Gorrie and what markets do they serve?",
        "body": "Department of Homeland Security is the top buyer of Brasfield and Gorrie work at $326M in FY2026 to date. Brasfield and Gorrie also sold to the Department of Defense for $59.6M and to the General Services Administration for $21.1M, with additional smaller obligations to the Department of Justice and NASA. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is Brasfield and Gorrie’s primary NAICS market at $416M, with minimal federal obligations recorded in Engineering Services and other construction NAICS."
      }
    ]
